ring.prompt:
A sprite sheet for a game VFX artist: the frame-by-frame animation of ONE effect for a commercial PC rhythm game, at the finish level of a top commercial action game's hand-painted VFX flipbooks.

LAYOUT: exactly 16 frames in a 4 x 4 grid of equal square cells, read left to right, top to bottom (frame 1 top-left, frame 16 bottom-right). Pure black background (#000000) everywhere. NO grid lines, NO borders, NO frame numbers, NO text. The effect is centred on the same point in every cell and stays inside its cell with black space around it; nothing touches a cell edge.

THE EFFECT: the SHOCKWAVE of a heavy seal being stamped down at the centre of the cell, seen flat from the front. The seal itself is NOT drawn: only the ring of force and light that runs out from where it lands. Every element is white and grey light only, with no colour at all, because the game colours it itself.

THE ANIMATION, one continuous motion across the 16 frames:
- frames 1-2: a small blinding round flash at the centre with a thin bright ring just leaving it;
- frames 3-5: the ring is a thick, bright, perfectly circular shockwave running outward fast, with short radial streaks and specks of dust thrown ahead of it;
- frames 6-10: the ring has grown to most of the cell and is thinner, it breaks into separate arcs, a second, fainter, thinner ring follows it inside, and the specks fly on outward;
- frames 11-14: only thin broken arcs near the edge of the effect and a few specks are left, fading;
- frames 15-16: almost nothing, the last faint arc; frame 16 is black.

Every frame is a different drawing of the same event a moment later: shapes change, break up and travel outward, they are not one picture scaled up. Painterly, energetic, with sharp bright edges and soft glow. It is light only, on black, to be added onto the screen. No ground, no objects, no characters, no logos, no letters, no numbers.

